red":1},{"he":"האריות אוכלים ארנבים.","en":"The lions are eating rabbits.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הפיל רואֶה את הילדות.","en":"The elephant sees the girls.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"התפוחים טעימים, תודה!","en":"The apples are tasty, thank you!","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/f874697f1fdb06d583b75d7622a30ae3"},{"he":"סוסים לא שותים את זה!","en":"Horses do not drink this!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אני אוהב לאכול תפוזים.","en":"I love eating oranges.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ברווזות לא שותות בירה.","en":"Female ducks do not drink beer.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"החתולים שותים את החלב.","en":"The cats are drinking the milk.","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/e9aaae27000b5a0c2d62a0431c4530f0"},{"he":"הכלב רואֶה את החתולות.","en":"The dog sees the female cats.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"בקרוב, אריות צמחוניים!","en":"Soon, vegetarian lions!","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"הכלבות אוכלות את האוכל.","en":"The female dogs are eating the food.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אנחנו אוכלים את הגבינות.","en":"We are eating the cheeses.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הברווזים לא רוצים לאכול.","en":"The ducks do not want to eat.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"סוסים אוהבים לאכול סוכר.","en":"Horses love to eat sugar.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"ברווזים אוהבים לאכול לחם.","en":"Ducks like to eat bread.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הפילים אוכלים את הכריכים.","en":"The elephants are eating the sandwiches.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"הוא קורא עיתונים או ספרים?","en":"Is he reading newspapers or books?","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/3d9352c0bec72fc46421a729103275f0"},{"he":"כלבים וחתולים הם חיות מחמד.","en":"Dogs and cats are pets.","alt":[],"t":"t"}],"hints":{"פרות":"cow / cows","הספרים":"the books / the books are","אין":"not has / not have / nothing can be done","דרכים":"road, way, path / roads","חיות":"animals / animal","יפים":"beautiful (pl. masc.) / handsome / nice","העוגות":"the cakes / the cakes are","יפות":"beautiful / pretty / beautiful (f.p)","יש":"I have / do you have / has","לה":"her / it (feminine nouns) / she has","סוסים":"horses / horse (Stallion)","להם":"them / they do not have / to them","צבים":"turtle, tortoise / turtles","לו":"if / if (cond.) / to him","לי":"I have / for me / me","כלבים":"dog / dogs","שמחים":"happy (m.p)","לנו":"for us / to us / us","כלבות":"dogs (f.p)","צלחות":"plate, dish / plates","ספרים":"books / book","טעימות":"tasty (f.p)","טעימים":"are delicious / are tasty / tasty (pl. masc.)","לךָ":"to you / you / do you have","חתולים":"cat / cats","אוכלות":"are eating / eat / eating","ברווזות":"ducks (f.p)","אבא":"dad / father / father, dad","קורא":"is reading / read / reading","לכם":"do you have / to you (pl. masc.) / you","ציפורים":"bird / birds","עיתונים":"newspapers / newspaper","ברווזים":"duck (Drake) / duck / ducks","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","תפוחים":"apples / apple","רואֶה":"is seeing / see / sees","שותֶה":"drink / drinking / drinks","בירות":"beer / beers","את":"it / that / the fruit","אוכלת":"are eating / eating / is eating","כריכים":"sandwich / sandwiches","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","תפוזים":"oranges / orange (Fruit)","מים":"water","הציפורים":"the birds","או":"or","אנחנו":"we / we are / we (c.p)","שותים":"are drinking / drink / drinking","מיץ":"a glass of juice / juice","אריות":"lion / lions","אוהבים":"like / love / love(s) (m.p - pres.)","בשר":"meat / meat, flesh","חתולות":"cat / cats (f.p)","חלב":"milk","אוכלים":"are eating / eat / eating","אתם":"do you want / you / you are","החתול":"the cat","אוהב":"like / likes / love","גבינות":"cheese / cheeses","רוצות":"want (f.p - pres.)","לאכול":"eat / eating / to eat","פירות":"fruit","רוצים":"do you want / want / want (m.p - pres.)","סוסות":"horse (Mare) / horses (f.p)","הנשים":"the women","אוהבות":"love(s) (f.p - pres.)","התפוחים":"the apples","עוגות":"cake / cakes","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","לחם":"bread","יינות":"wine / wines","סליחה":"I am sorry / pardon / excuse me","עברית":"Hebrew","ארנבים":"rabbit / hare","תודה":"thank you / thanks","זה":"it / it is / it's","בירה":"beer","החתולים":"the cats","החלב":"milk / the milk / the milk is","הכלב":"the dog","בקרוב":"soon, shortly","האוכל":"the food","סוכר":"sugar","הם":"are / they / they are"},"words":[{"he":"או","en":"or","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"o"},{"he":"קורא","en":"read","alt":["is reading","reading"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"kore"},{"he":"עיתונים","en":"newspapers","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"iton"},{"he":"ספרים","en":"books","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"sefer"},{"he":"התפוחים","en":"the apples","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"טעימים","en":"are tasty","alt":["are delicious","tasty (pl. masc.)"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"t'imim"},{"he":"הספרים","en":"the books","alt":["the books are"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"יפים","en":"nice","alt":["beautiful (pl. masc.)","handsome"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"yafim"},{"he":"החתולים","en":"the cats","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"שותים","en":"drinking","alt":["are drinking","drink"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shotim"},{"he":"סוסות","en":"Horse (Mare)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"susah"},{"he":"צבים","en":"Turtle, Tortoise","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"tzav"},{"he":"יינות","en":"Wine","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"yayin"},{"he":"אריות","en":"Lion","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"aryeh"},{"he":"ברווזות","en":"Ducks (f.p)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"bar'vazot"},{"he":"חיות מחמד","en":"pet","alt":["pets"],"from":"skill","tr":"khayat"},{"he":"סוסים","en":"horses","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"sus"},{"he":"כלבות","en":"Dogs (f.p)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"k'lavot"},{"he":"חתולות","en":"Cat","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"khatulah"},{"he":"הוא","en":"he","alt":["(he) is","(it) is"],"from":"phrase","tr":"hu"},{"he":"תודה","en":"thanks","alt":["thank you"],"from":"phrase","tr":"todah"},{"he":"את","en":"you","alt":["the milk"],"from":"phrase","tr":"at"},{"he":"החלב","en":"milk","alt":["the milk","the milk","the milk is"],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["הסוסות","היינות","ודרכים","סוסות","ובירות","צבים","הבירות","יינות","הילדות","וכלבות","וחתולות","הכלבות","הברווזות","הסוסים","הספרים","האריות","אריות","ברווזות","חיות מחמד","סוסים","החתולות","כלבות","ספרים","חתולות"],"tips":"In Hebrew we have 2 endings for nouns in the plural form:\n\n**יִם**(im) - for masculine nouns.\n\n**וֹת**(ot) - for feminine nouns.\n\nIf the noun ends with the letter \"ה\" - we omit it before adding the plural ending.\n\nFor example:\n\n>פר**ה** (par**á**) - cow\n\n>פר**ות** (par**ót**) - cows\n\nIf the word ends with a letter in its final form, we replace it with the original form, and then add the plural ending.\n\nFor example: \n\n> עיתו**ן** (itón) - newspaper.\n\n> עיתו**נ**ים (itoním) - newspapers.\n\nThese are the basic rules. However, many masculine nouns have the feminine plural ending and vice versa. Unfortunately these irregular words are fairly unpredictable. For the most part you just have to learn them. \n\nFor example, יין (yain) - wine is a masculine noun, but the plural is יינות (yeinót). דבורה (dvorá) -bee- is a feminine noun, but the plural is דבורים (dvorím). Note that adjectives/verbs always agree with the gender of the noun regardless of its plural ending, so you would say *יינות טעימים - tasty wines* ; and not *יינות טעימות*. \n\n***\n\nWe also have nouns that have both masculine and feminine forms. These nouns usually refer to humans and animals.\n\nFor example:\n\n>חתול**ים** (khatul**ím**) - a male or mixed-gender group of cats (plural masculine).\n\n>חתול**ות** (khatul**ót**) - female cats (plural feminine)."}